 "about": "Every place that shows the glucose card or its value, per platform: the registry behind 'One graph everywhere' (CLAUDE.md). A 'card' surface draws card pixels only through the renderer (GlucoseCard.draw / GlucoseCard.image) and chooses only its size, its place's settings and the parts; a 'glyph' surface (text and icons the system lays out) takes the value, arrow and freshness from GlucoseCard.face. tools/check: card-surface (a file that calls the renderer must be the registered file of the surface it names), card-api (outside 'owners' only 'api' members of the renderer's objects). CardLayoutTest (Android) and -graphselftest (Mac) render ../layout/scenes.json through each surface's real entry path at its sizes and check ../layout/rules.json. Sizes are dp / pt of the surface's own box (see each surface's 'size').",
